{"diagnosis": "Loopback 0xa5 was never received so recv_buf_valid never asserted, causing TRAP uart timeout FAIL 0xdead. Expected recv_divcnt to increment each clk to time baud periods, but it stays at 0. Root cause is line 74 `recv_divcnt <= recv_divcnt + 0` which never counts, so condition `2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider` in state 1 never becomes true and recv_state stalls.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@
 			recv_buf_data <= 0;
 			recv_buf_valid <= 0;
 		end else begin
-			recv_divcnt <= recv_divcnt + 0;
+			recv_divcnt <= recv_divcnt + 1;
 			if (reg_dat_re)
 				recv_buf_valid <= 0;
 			case (recv_state)", "expected": "tohost PASS with 0xa5 loopback byte received, no uart timeout"}

